From: Yocto build fix
Subject: [PATCH] autoapp: send raw touch coordinates instead of scaling client-side

InputDevice::handleNativeTouchEvent() used to convert touchPoint.pos()
(the raw touch position, in Qt screen coordinates) into AndroidAuto's
negotiated video resolution via a client-side scale. Two different values
were tried for the scaling divisor across earlier fixes -- the video
widget's on-screen size (to invert its render-time squish) and the full
screen (assuming Qt's own touch normalization already handled everything)
-- and both were confirmed by direct on-device testing (tapping Contacts,
a call icon, and other UI elements) to still land touches on the wrong
element.

The actual working model turned out to be simpler: send touchPoint.pos()
through completely unscaled, and let AA map the declared touch surface
(InputService::fillFeatures' touch_screen_config, now set to the real
full-screen coordinate space by 0009) to its own rendered video resolution
internally. This matches how most touchscreen protocols separate
"declare your device's coordinate space once" from "report raw
coordinates in it" -- the client-side scale-up this code used to do was
redundant with (and inconsistent against) whatever AA already does
internally with the declared touch_screen_config, not something AA was
relying on the host to do itself.

Confirmed by on-device testing: with this change (paired with 0009),
tapping application icons opens the correct one. Some imprecision remains
when icons are placed very close together, but that's ordinary
touch-target/spacing tolerance, not a systemic coordinate error like the
previous scaled variants exhibited.

touchscreenGeometry_ is retained on InputDevice only because
IInputDevice::getTouchscreenGeometry() (used solely for the
touch_screen_config declaration in InputService::fillFeatures) still reads
it; it is no longer read anywhere in the touch-dispatch path itself.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [oe-specific: this board's touch pipeline
needs raw passthrough, not host-side scaling, to align with AA's own
internal coordinate mapping]

diff --git a/src/autoapp/Projection/InputDevice.cpp b/src/autoapp/Projection/InputDevice.cpp
--- a/src/autoapp/Projection/InputDevice.cpp
+++ b/src/autoapp/Projection/InputDevice.cpp
@@ -291,9 +291,17 @@
         break;
     };
 
+    // Send raw touch-surface coordinates unscaled: AA maps the declared
+    // touch_screen_config (InputService::fillFeatures, via
+    // getTouchscreenGeometry() -- see ServiceFactory.cpp) to its own
+    // rendered video resolution internally. Scaling here client-side (as
+    // this used to, against either the video widget's on-screen size or
+    // the full screen) is redundant with that and was confirmed by
+    // on-device testing (tapping application icons) to land touches on the
+    // wrong element regardless of which rect was used as the divisor.
     const QTouchEvent::TouchPoint& touchPoint = touch->touchPoints().first();
-    const uint32_t x = (static_cast<float>(touchPoint.pos().x()) / touchscreenGeometry_.width()) * displayGeometry_.width();
-    const uint32_t y = (static_cast<float>(touchPoint.pos().y()) / touchscreenGeometry_.height()) * displayGeometry_.height();
+    const uint32_t x = static_cast<uint32_t>(touchPoint.pos().x());
+    const uint32_t y = static_cast<uint32_t>(touchPoint.pos().y());
     OPENAUTO_LOG(info) << "[InputDevice] dispatching NATIVE touch x=" << x << " y=" << y
                         << " rawPos=(" << touchPoint.pos().x() << "," << touchPoint.pos().y() << ")";
     eventHandler_->onTouchEvent({type, x, y, 0});
